description: >-
  The vision, mission, and pillars of the Human Building Synergy Laboratory
  (HUBS) at the University of Arizona.
---
{% from "icons.njk" import icon %}

<section class="pageHero wrap">
  <p class="label">About the lab</p>
  <h1>
    <span class="c-hu">HU</span>man <span class="c-bl">B</span>uilding
    <span class="c-ai">S</span>ynergy Laboratory
  </h1>
  <p class="lede">{{ site.researchArea }}.</p>
</section>

<section class="band band--tight wrap">
  <div class="prose">
    <p class="label">Vision</p>
    <h2 style="margin-top:.5rem">Buildings that understand the people in them — and can be argued with.</h2>
    <p style="font-size:1.15rem;color:var(--ink-2)">
      HUBS works toward built environments that understand their occupants well
      enough to act on their behalf, and explain themselves well enough to be
      trusted. That takes three things at once: a building that senses without
      intruding, an agent that reasons under real constraints, and an occupant who
      keeps the last word.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band--rule band--tight wrap">
  <div class="band__head measure">
    <p class="label">Mission</p>
    <h2>The questions we keep asking.</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      One question per corner of the triangle, and one that belongs to all three.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="grid grid--2">
    <div class="card">
      <p class="card__head c-hu">Of the human</p>
      <ul>
        <li>How do people express what they need from a space?</li>
        <li>What do those words actually mean, for that particular person?</li>
        <li>What makes someone trust an automated system enough to leave it on?</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <p class="card__head c-ai">Of the AI</p>
      <ul>
        <li>When should an agent act on its own judgment, and when must it defer?</li>
        <li>How does it arbitrate between occupants who want opposite things?</li>
        <li>What does an explanation have to contain to be worth anything?</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <p class="card__head c-bl">Of the building</p>
      <ul>
        <li>How can systems sense occupants non-invasively and effortlessly?</li>
        <li>How can a space be conditioned at the scale of a person, not a zone?</li>
        <li>How does a building report its own limits and failures honestly?</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <p class="card__head">Of all three</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Who gets the last word when they disagree?</li>
        <li>Who pays when comfort is traded for grid flexibility?</li>
        <li>What happens to the direct human–building relationship in between?</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band--rule band--tight wrap">
  <div class="band__head measure">
    <p class="label">Pillars</p>
    <h2>What holds the work up.</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="grid grid--2">
    <div class="card">
      <p class="card__head c-hu">Human agency</p>
      <p class="muted">
        The occupant keeps authority. An override is the most valuable signal the
        system receives, not a failure of it.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <p class="card__head c-ai">Machine reasoning</p>
      <p class="muted">
        Agents that plan under real constraints — grid, cost, physics, other
        people — and can say what they did and why.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <p class="card__head c-bl">Physical embodiment</p>
      <p class="muted">
        Sensing and actuation that reach the scale of a single person, and report
        back what actually happened.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <p class="card__head">Synergy</p>
      <p class="muted">
        Comfort and energy treated as a win-win to be engineered, not a trade-off
        to be split.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band--rule band--tight wrap">
  <div class="cta">
    <p class="label">Next</p>
    <h2 style="margin-top:.8rem">See what the questions have produced.</h2>
    <div class="btnRow">
      <a class="btn" href="/research/">Research {{ icon("arrow-right") }}</a>
      <a class="btn btn--quiet" href="/facility/">The facility</a>
      <a class="btn btn--quiet" href="/join-us/">Join us</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

